  "description": "NEMXEM crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C96 H82 Cu2 Gd4 N6 O24,C1 H2 Cl2. From the CIF bond table, Gd4 (Gd) has 7 O neighbors; Gd3 (Gd) has 7 O neighbors; Cu2 (Cu) has 4 O neighbors; Gd5 (Gd) has 7 O neighbors; Gd6 (Gd) has 7 O neighbors; Cu3 (Cu) has 4 O neighbors; Gd1 (Gd) has 7 O neighbors; Gd2 (Gd) has 7 O neighbors; Cu1 (Cu) has 4 O neighbors; Gd7 (Gd) has 7 O neighbors; Gd8 (Gd) has 7 O neighbors; Cu4 (Cu) has 4 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 14 pairs, 2 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.375-3.944 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 97.30-113.45°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C97H82Cl2Cu2Gd4N6O24.",
